-- title:
--   Kummer descent: cyclic unramified cover of a node of thickness mn
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a commutative Noetherian local domain that is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $m,n$ be positive natural numbers with $m$ and $n$ units in $W$ and such that $W$ contains a primitive $(mn)$-th root of unity. Write $R_0 = \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^{mn})$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{mn}$, and let $\mathrm{const}$ denote the map sending $w \in W$ to the class of the constant $w$. Let $B$ be an integrally closed Noetherian local domain that is an $R_0$-algebra, module-finite over $R_0$ and with $R_0$ acting faithfully. Let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $R_0$ and $F$ a field which is simultaneously an extension of $K_0$ and a fraction field of $B$, all structure maps compatible, with $F/K_0$ finite Galois of degree $n$ and with cyclic Galois group. Assume further that $B$ is unramified over $R_0$ at every prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $B$ whose contraction to $R_0$ has height $1$, and that every $b \in B$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $B$ to the image of $\mathrm{const}(\pi^{mn})(w)$ for some $w \in W$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $e : B \to \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^{m}) = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{m})$ carrying, for every $w \in W$, the image in $B$ of $\mathrm{const}(\pi^{mn})(w)$ to $\mathrm{const}(\pi^{m})(w)$. The conclusion asserts a ring isomorphism compatible with constants from $W$, not a priori an $R_0$-algebra isomorphism.
--
--   This is the Kummer-descent (Abhyankar-type) normalisation statement for the completed local ring at a node: a normal local cover of the thickness-$mn$ crossing $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{mn})$ which is cyclic of degree $n$, unramified in height one and trivial on residue constants is again a crossing, of thickness $m$. It is used by the variant [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isUnit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isUnit), in the analysis of the local structure of modular curves at supersingular/cuspidal crossings.
